1. DEFINITIONS
================================================================================

1.1  "Materials" means, collectively, the Software, the Specification and the
     Documentation, in every version and release, in every medium, and every
     Modification of them.

1.2  "Software" means all computer code in any form: source code, object code,
     executables, libraries, packages, scripts, notebooks, build and
     configuration files, infrastructure-as-code, database schemas and
     migrations, templates, agent instructions and policy files, and the tests,
     examples and data files distributed with them.

1.3  "Specification" means the architectural specifications, interface
     definitions, schemas, state machines, conformance tests and diagrams that
     the Licensor publishes under this License, including every document in the
     repository "ultrastable/spec".

1.4  "Documentation" means all other written or visual material the Licensor
     publishes under this License, including guides, concept documents, case
     studies and README files.

1.5  "Source Code" means the preferred form of the Software for making
     modifications, including the build scripts and configuration needed to
     build, install and run it. "Object Code" means any other form.

1.6  "Modification" means any change to a file of the Materials, and any new
     file that contains a substantial portion of a file of the Materials. A
     separate file that You write and that does not copy from the Materials is
     not a Modification merely because it calls, imports, links to or
     communicates with the Software.

1.7  "Covered Files" means the files of the Materials and all Modifications.
     "Larger Work" means a work that combines Covered Files with files that are
     not Covered Files.

1.8  "Distribute" means to make a copy of the Materials, a Modification or a
     Larger Work available to anyone other than You, by any means, including
     publishing a repository, package, container image or download.

1.9  "Network Use" means letting anyone other than You interact with the
     Software, a Modification or a Larger Work remotely through a computer
     network.

1.10 "Commercial Use" has the meaning in Section 3.

1.11 "Implementation" means any software, service, system or product, written by
     anyone, that implements, in whole or in substantial part, the architecture,
     interfaces, schemas, state machines or behaviors described in the
     Specification.

1.12 "Commercial Terms" means the Licensor's then-current published price list
     and terms for Commercial Licenses, currently the file COMMERCIAL-TERMS.md in
     the repository "ultrastable/license".

1.13 "Commercial License" means a license for Commercial Use granted by the
     Licensor under Section 4, either by acceptance of the Commercial Terms or by
     a separate written agreement signed by the Licensor.

1.14 "Covered Revenue" has the meaning given in the Commercial Terms. In
     general it means money and the market value of other consideration received
     by You or Your Affiliates from any product, service, deliverable or
     organization that is operated, managed, produced or run with material use
     of the Materials or of an Implementation.

1.15 "Affiliate" means any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under
     common control with You. "You" means the individual or entity exercising
     rights under this License, together with its Affiliates.

