3. COMMERCIAL USE REQUIRES A COMMERCIAL LICENSE
================================================================================

3.1  Any use of the Materials or of an Implementation that generates money is
     Commercial Use and requires a Commercial License. This includes any use
     that earns revenue for, saves money for, or forms part of the operations of
     a for-profit person or organization. Without limitation, Commercial Use
     includes:
     (a) selling, renting, licensing or sublicensing the Materials, or charging
         for access to, hosting of, installation of or support for them;
     (b) offering the Software, or functionality substantially provided by it or
         by an Implementation, as or within a paid product, hosted service
         (software-as-a-service), API, application or platform, including a free
         product or service that is monetized through advertising, data
         collection, subscriptions, upselling or investment;
     (c) using the Materials to run, manage, staff, direct or improve a business
         or any other organization that earns revenue, including an
         organization operated autonomously or by AI agents, and including a
         business started, grown or operated with the Software from an idea;
     (d) using the Materials to produce deliverables, results, analyses or
         services for which You or anyone else is paid, including consulting,
         contracting and freelance work;
     (e) any use by or for a for-profit entity, including internal operations,
         research and development, testing, training of employees and
         production use, subject only to the evaluation allowance in Section
         2.2(e);
     (f) embedding the Materials or an Implementation in, or bundling them with,
         hardware, devices or other products that are sold or leased;
     (g) using the Materials or their outputs to train, fine-tune or evaluate a
         commercial artificial-intelligence or code-generation model, system or
         service (Section 9 applies); and
     (h) any other use in which the Materials or an Implementation contribute to
         revenue, investment value, market position or cost savings for any
         person or organization.

3.2  A person who is paid to use the Materials for someone else's benefit is
     engaged in Commercial Use even if that person owns no business.

3.3  Where a use is partly commercial, the whole use is Commercial Use.

