     sanctions or export control rules prohibit the dealing.

4.2  Separate agreements. The Licensor may grant custom commercial licenses,
     including perpetual, revenue-share, field-limited, territory-limited,
     time-limited and public-benefit-conditional licenses, by a written
     agreement signed by the Licensor. The Licensor is not obliged to grant any
     particular custom license.

4.3  Changes to Commercial Terms. The Licensor may change the Commercial Terms
     for new Commercial Licenses at any time. A change does not increase the
     price or reduce the rights of a Commercial License already in force until
     its renewal date, if it has one, or twelve (12) months after notice,
     whichever is later.

4.4  No implied license. Nothing in this License, no course of dealing, and no
     silence or failure to respond by the Licensor grants an implied Commercial
     License, a waiver or an estoppel. Commercial Use is licensed only under
     Section 4.1 or 4.2.

4.5  A Commercial License covers use of Modifications and Larger Works to the
     extent it says so. It does not remove the duties in Sections 6, 8, 9 and
